# Fork release contract for v0.53.0: macOS artifacts are unsigned and not
# notarized. verify-macos-binary.sh proves that mechanically — it accepts only
# an absent signature or Go's pure adhoc,linker-signed output, and rejects any
# identity-bearing signature, authority, secure timestamp, or notarization.
# Release provenance records signing:"none".
#
# Signed Apple publication is a separate release-contract upgrade: it requires
# provisioning a real Developer ID identity and a source change to the compiled
# embedded-VMD trust policy. Only then do the managed signing/notary fields
# return here, carrying the fork's own identity.
CRABBOX_RELEASE_APPLE_SIGNING='none'
